Z||000001||trigger||05-31-2001||07:33 PM||||Ok. I'm not positive, but it sounds like somebody tried to use that switch to manually turn on the fan.  I know some people do this, but I'm not sure if it helps.  My car has never overheated before.  Does every thing on the car work.  Does the fan work, by itself, or with the switch, or at all?  A guy in my Fiero club bought a low mileage, decent shape fiero for pretty cheap.  The previous owner had unplugged all the sensors, and wrapped them in aluminum.  He had cut wires and everything.  He let all the freon out of the A/C and stuff like that.  He was trying to keep the "aliens" out.  I'm not making this up.  The new owner plugged all the sensors back in and drove it.  He still finds cut wires once and a while.  Ok, now that I'm done rattling on, I hope my advice can help in some way.  Let me know if you need any more help.  My e-mail is mumbles7@yahoo.com<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
