Z||000008||mrgone||06-05-2001||02:27 AM||||also this made me think<P>"why did he splice up wires like that"<P>my coolent temp guage doesnt work....<BR>so prolly the thing that sends the command to the fan to turn on is busted?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tigger||06-05-2001||08:30 AM||||My reply in the other post:<BR><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007808.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007808.html</A><P>No, chances are just the temp gauge sensor is busted, the radiator fan is turned on/off by another sensor.<P>The temp sensor for the gauge is located on the cyl head if this is a 4 cyl.  It's on the forward driver's side corner and sticks straight up.  To test the circuit, disconnect the plug and ground it using a paperclip and the gauge will peg telling you that the sensor is bad, wiring good.  Before you replace the sensor check for corrosion on the connections.<P>Read up on this: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007399.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007399.html</A><P>I believe the radiator fan turn on/off sensor is also located on the driver's side of the head, but points forward, towards the driver's seat.  Grounding that circuit when everything is back together correctly should turn the radiator fan on.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||1
